      "text": "   \n\n*4 is **not** a \"clock equivalent'' number, because 4*4 is not an elapsed time (36) on a clock.*~$4$* is \"clock equivalent'' yet 4 is not the smallest one.*\n*5 is also **not** a \"clock equivalent'' number, because 5*5 is not an elapsed time (25) on a clock.*~$5$* is \"clock equivalent'' yet 5 is not the smallest one.*\n*6 is also **not** a \"clock equivalent'' number, because 6*6 is not an elapsed time (36) on a clock.*~5 is \"clock equivalent'' yet 6 is not the smallest one.*\n*7 is also **not** a \"clock equivalent'' number, because 7*7 is not an elapsed time (49) on a clock.*\n\nTherefore, ~$8$* is the smallest \"clock equivalent'' number.![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/2024_05_01_ea5c44b1998680003d90g-138.jpg?height=222&width=490&top_left_y=1928&top_left_x=1018).",
